  <h2>Compatibility:
    {% set cs = compat.status if compat and compat.status else (a.compatibility_status or "unknown") %}
    <span class="record-pill" style="background:{% if cs == 'native' %}#2f4a3a{% elif cs == 'plausible' %}#5a4a1f{% elif cs == 'incompatible' %}#5a1f1f{% else %}#444{% endif %};">{{ cs }}</span>
  </h2>
  {% if cs == 'native' %}
  <p>All organs come from one source strategy — this is the original organism. The compiled artifact is the existing monolithic <code>.py</code>; it runs as authored. No graft to validate.</p>
  {% elif cs == 'incompatible' %}
  <p>This cross-genome graft is <strong>blocked</strong>: the exit/management organs need things the chosen entry does not provide. The compiler refuses to emit code for an incompatible graft (audit §9.3).</p>
  {% elif cs == 'plausible' %}
  <p>This graft is <strong>plausible but unverified</strong> — no missing columns or custom_data were detected, but that does not prove it works. It is <em>ready for generation</em>; code generation + a validity-gated backtest come next.</p>
  {% else %}
  <p>Not yet compiled.</p>
  {% endif %}
  {% if compat and compat.findings %}
  <ul>{% for f in compat.findings %}<li><small>{{ f }}</small></li>{% endfor %}</ul>
  {% endif %}
  {% if compat and (compat.missing_indicators or compat.missing_custom_data) %}
  <div class="kv-grid">
    {% if compat.missing_indicators %}<div><span>Missing indicators</span><strong><small>{{ compat.missing_indicators | join(", ") }}</small></strong></div>{% endif %}
    {% if compat.missing_custom_data %}<div><span>Missing custom_data</span><strong><small>{{ compat.missing_custom_data | join(", ") }}</small></strong></div>{% endif %}
  </div>
  {% endif %}
  <form method="post" action="/assemblies/{{ a.slug }}/compile" style="margin-top:0.5rem;">
    <button type="submit">Re-run compatibility gate</button>
  </form>
</section>

